		)
		(uuid "9b8ed450-ed5c-de0a-c2e8-bb51bfd82653")
	)
	(text "U401 RTL8211F-CG: one chip, drawn as RGMII side (A), line side (B) and power (C)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 127 62.23 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "9e6e5b28-1a65-0fbf-788c-329dccdc9e55")
	)
	(text "MDIO, INTB, RST: 4.7 k up\n(MDIO's 1.5 k is for a long bus)\nRST: 330 Ω + 1 µF, ~10 ms after power"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 62.23 121.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.85 0.85)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b701c1e7-d8ee-8fcd-bd57-22fceda753a2")
	)
	(text "100 Ω differential pairs; P on the transformer's - ends, N on its + ends, both sides (see the layout)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 189.23 201.93 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.85 0.85)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c8ecdd22-7e57-961e-6512-3d5e1299f03e")
	)
	(text_box "+3V3_ETH is +3V3 through a ferrite bead (power sheet). The PHY address strap is the default (RXD3 pulled up internally): PHYAD = 1. RXD1 pulled up (4.7 k): TXDLY\n= 1; RXD0 at its internal pull-up: RXDLY = 1 -- both 2 ns RGMII delays inside the PHY, so the gateware adds none (LiteEth tx_delay = rx_delay = 0)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 330.2 335.28 0)
		(size 120.65 6.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.95 0.95)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8e0ed234-6aa9-92ba-13a1-478a304a8591")
	)
	(text_box "The FPGA talks RGMII (4-bit DDR at 125 MHz) at 3.3 V to the PHY; 22 Ω series resistors damp the lines. The PHY makes its own 1.0 V core with an internal switcher (REG_OUT, 2.2 µH). Straps on the LED pins are sampled at reset: CFG_EXT = 1 (external 3.3 V on DVDD_RG) and CFG_LDO[1:0] = 00 (3.3 V I/O pads), PHY address 1, TX delay off, RX delay on (the gateware's RGMII PHY expects the 2 ns\nreceive delay in the PHY and adds its own transmit delay). The magnetics are a G2406S module: each chip-side centre tap gets its own 100 nF to ground, as a voltage-mode driver wants; the line-side taps go to a Bob Smith termination (75 Ω each, 1 nF / 3 kV 1812 to ground)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 25.4 0)
		(size 340.36 6.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fedb86bf-910e-ef94-be58-73e17360988b")
	)
